# The Dockerfile's build stage runs `npm ci` (which
# installs strictly from package-lock.json) and then `COPY . .`. Without this
# file, `COPY . .` layers the host's own node_modules/.next/out over that
# fresh install inside the image, so whatever happens to be sitting on the
# developer's machine (a stale build, a different platform's native binary,
# an out-of-date dependency tree) can silently ship instead of what npm ci
# just resolved. Excluding them forces the image to always contain exactly
# what npm ci produced from package-lock.json.
node_modules
server/.venv
server/tests
server/.pytest_cache
**/__pycache__
*.pyc
*.tsbuildinfo
.next
out
npm-debug.log*
